<section class="pkg-faq-band">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="pkg-faq">
      <details><summary>How do I start the conversation about moving with my parent?</summary><p>Begin with what they want from their next home rather than what the family has decided. Listen first, involve them in each decision and agree a timeline together. A Discovery Consultation from &pound;150 can include your parent and family in building the plan.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you manage the move if I live far away?</summary><p>Yes. Your dedicated coordinator handles the work on the ground and keeps you updated by phone or email, so you do not need to be there for every step.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you work with my parent directly and keep the family updated separately?</summary><p>Yes. We work with the person who is moving and keep family members informed to whatever degree suits your family.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if we are not sure how much support is needed?</summary><p>A Discovery Consultation, from &pound;150, gives you an honest view of the situation and a written plan, timeline and budget before you commit to a package.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How much does it cost to move an elderly parent?</summary><p>Packages start at &pound;995 for packing and removals and &pound;1,850 for a full-service move. The right one depends on the size of the home and how much support is needed.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

